ument, from, to, asOf) -> List.of(\n81\t                        new FundingRatePoint(Instant.parse(\"2026-05-20T08:00:00Z\"), new BigDecimal(\"0.012\")),\n82\t                        new FundingRatePoint(Instant.parse(\"2026-06-20T08:00:00Z\"), new BigDecimal(\"0.008\"))));\n83\t        AssessIncomeCliRunner runner = new AssessIncomeCliRunner(\n84\t                service, new PrintStream(bytes, true, StandardCharsets.UTF_8));\n85\t        runner.run(new DefaultApplicationArguments(arguments));\n86\t        return new Invocation(runner.getExitCode(), bytes.toString(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));\n87\t    }\n88\t\n89\t    private static String[] completeArgu..."},"call_e66a7a7e7e7543f0adb6d72f":{"tool_use_id":"call_e66a7a7e7e7543f0adb6d72f","tool_name":"Read CLAUDE.md","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"1\t# CLAUDE.md\n2\t\n3\tThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n4\t\n5\t## Project Status\n6\t\n7\tPhase 1's first data slice is implemented and peer-review hardening is complete: OKX public funding-rate history is validated into typed observations and atomically persisted as append-only facts with a successful execution. Logical `funding_sync_request` and immutable `analysis_run` executions are separate. A minimal `sync-market` CLI is implemented (single-page `latest`, cursor `backfill` over `[from,to)` with persisted page ledger/checkpoint/resume and honest coverage states, read-only `stale-list`, explicitly confirmed `stale-recover` with expected-run-id fencing; stale age is judged by MySQL `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)`, never the JVM clock). Scheduling, cross-interval integrity checks, account fee data, and private/read-only account APIs are not implemented. `docs/` remains the authoritative product specification; read it before extending the code:\n8\t\n9\t- `docs/README.md` — goals, principles, tech stack, V1 tool plan, phased rollout\n10\t- `docs/01-Income-Source.md` — income source definitions, lifecycle, backtest requirements\n11\t- `docs/02-Portfolio.md` — portfolio allocation rules, Incremental Net Benefit formula, scaling gates\n12\t- `docs/03-AI-Advisor.md` — AI advisor/researcher scope and boundaries\n13\t\n14\tDocumentation is written in Chinese; keep it that way.\n15\t\n16\t## What This Project Is\n17\t\n18\tA local, read-only personal tool for managing ~200,000 USDT of crypto income via existing OKX products (funding-rate arbitrage, simple earn, spot grid). Target: 10–20% long-term annualized net return. It is **not** a trading platform: no automated trading, AI never touches trade/withdrawal permissions, and the user executes all actions manually on OKX.\n19\t\n20\tCore priorities, in order: **赚钱第一 (real net return), 工程第二 (engineering only where it moves return), AI 第三 (AI advises, never decides)**. The system's most frequent recommendation should be \"hold\" (保持).\n21\t\n22\t## Implemented Tech Stack\n23\t\n24\t- JDK 25 + Spring Boot 4.1.0 + Maven, single monolith (`app.cryptoincome` base package)\n25\t- MySQL 8.4 LTS via official Docker image (`compose.yaml`); app connects with the business user, not root; connections use UTC\n26\t- MyBatis-Plus 3.5.17 via `mybatis-plus-spring-boot4-starter` and `mybatis-plus-bom` — do NOT separately add MyBatis / `mybatis-spring-boot-starter` / MyBatis-Spring (dependency conflicts)\n27\t- Flyway is the only schema-migration path; no auto DDL\n28\t- JDK `HttpClient` + Jackson for OKX public and read-only account APIs\n29\t- JUnit 5 + Testcontainers MySQL for tests against real MySQL behavior\n30\t- Money: `BigDecimal`. Time: UTC `Instant`. Funding intervals follow actual `fundingTime`, never assumed 8h\n31\t- Deliberately excluded for V1: JPA, Spring Batch, message queues, microservices, real-time dashboards. Spring AI is added last, in an isolated adapter\n32\t\n33\t## Architecture Rules (from the design docs — these are constraints, not suggestions)\n34\t\n35\t- **Layering**: domain services depend only on project-defined Repository interfaces (for example `AnalysisRunRepository`), never on `BaseMapper` directly. MyBatis-Plus handles simple single-table CRUD; cash-flow attribution, income aggregation, backtest queries, and `analysis_run` state transitions use reviewable Mapper XML / explicit SQL. Business rules live in domain services, not in the ORM layer.\n36\t- **Three portfolio types must be kept separate**: Backtest / Shadow / Live, distinguished by `mode` + `run_id` with DB constraints forbidding cross-mode references. Live Portfolio can only be updated from OKX account snapshots and human-confirmed cash flows — never derived from backtest, shadow, or AI output.\n37\t- **Facts are append-only**: corrections insert new records; never silently overwrite history.\n38\t- Funding facts use a restricted mapper that exposes insertion and reads only; do not replace it with `BaseMapper`, bec..."},"output":"1\t# CLAUDE.md\n2\t\n3\tThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n4\t\n5\t## Project Status\n6\t\n7\tPhase 1's first data slice is implemented and peer-review hardening is complete: OKX public funding-rate history is validated into typed observations and atomically persisted as append-only facts with a successful execution. Logical `funding_sync_request` and immutable `analysis_run` executions are separate. A minimal `sync-market` CLI is implemented (single-page `latest`, cursor `backfill` over `[from,to)` with persisted page ledger/checkpoint/resume and honest coverage states, read-only `stale-list`, explicitly confirmed `stale-recover` with expected-run-id fencing; stale age is judged by MySQL `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)`, never the JVM clock). Scheduling, cross-interval integrity checks, account fee data, and private/read-only account APIs are not implemented. `docs/` remains the authoritative product specification; read it before extending the code:\n8\t\n9\t- `docs/README.md` — goals, principles, tech stack, V1 tool plan, phased rollout\n10\t- `docs/01-Income-Source.md` — income source definitions, lifecycle, backtest requirements\n11\t- `docs/02-Portfolio.md` — portfolio allocation rules, Incremental Net Benefit formula, scaling gates\n12\t- `docs/03-AI-Advisor.md` — AI advisor/researcher scope and boundaries\n13\t\n14\tDocumentation is written in Chinese; keep it that way.\n15\t\n16\t## What This Project Is\n17\t\n18\tA local, read-only personal tool for managing ~200,000 USDT of crypto income via existing OKX products (funding-rate arbitrage, simple earn, spot grid). Target: 10–20% long-term annualized net return. It is **not** a trading platform: no automated trading, AI never touches trade/withdrawal permissions, and the user executes all actions manually on OKX.\n19\t\n20\tCore priorities, in order: **赚钱第一 (real net return), 工程第二 (engineering only where it moves return), AI 第三 (AI advises, never decides)**. The system's most frequent recommendation should be \"hold\" (保持).\n21\t\n22\t## Implemented Tech Stack\n23\t\n24\t- JDK 25 + Spring Boot 4.1.0 + Maven, single monolith (`app.cryptoincome` base package)\n25\t- MySQL 8.4 LTS via official Docker image (`compose.yaml`); app connects with the business user, not root; connections use UTC\n26\t- MyBatis-Plus 3.5.17 via `mybatis-plus-spring-boot4-starter` and `mybatis-plus-bom` — do NOT separately add MyBatis / `mybatis-spring-boot-starter` / MyBatis-Spring (dependency conflicts)\n27\t- Flyway is the only schema-migration path; no auto DDL\n28\t- JDK `HttpClient` + Jackson for OKX public and read-only account APIs\n29\t- JUnit 5 + Testcontainers MySQL for tests against real MySQL behavior\n30\t- Money: `BigDecimal`. Time: UTC `Instant`. Funding intervals follow actual `fundingTime`, never assumed 8h\n31\t- Deliberately excluded for V1: JPA, Spring Batch, message queues, microservices, real-time dashboards. Spring AI is added last, in an isolated adapter\n32\t\n33\t## Architecture Rules (from the design docs — these are constraints, not suggestions)\n34\t\n35\t- **Layering**: domain services depend only on project-defined Repository interfaces (for example `AnalysisRunRepository`), never on `BaseMapper` directly. MyBatis-Plus handles simple single-table CRUD; cash-flow attribution, income aggregation, backtest queries, and `analysis_run` state transitions use reviewable Mapper XML / explicit SQL. Business rules live in domain services, not in the ORM layer.\n36\t- **Three portfolio types must be kept separate**: Backtest / Shadow / Live, distinguished by `mode` + `run_id` with DB constraints forbidding cross-mode references. Live Portfolio can only be updated from OKX account snapshots and human-confirmed cash flows — never derived from backtest, shadow, or AI output.\n37\t- **Facts are append-only**: corrections insert new records; never silently overwrite history.\n38\t- Funding facts use a restricted mapper that exposes insertion and reads only; do not replace it with `BaseMapper`, bec..."},"call_52951f4a1b244f609581372b":{"tool_use_id":"call_52951f4a1b244f609581372b","tool_name":"Read docs/09-Phase-1-Test-Runbook.md (1 - 60)","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"1\t# 第一期测试手册\n2\t\n3\t> 适用范围：简单赚币与 BTC 智能套利的 90 天收益评估。现货网格尚未实现，不在本手册验收范围内。\n4\t\n5\t## 1. 测试目标与边界\n6\t\n7\t本轮只验证四件事：\n8\t\n9\t1. 程序能正确读取 OKX 已实现资金费率事实；\n10\t2. 简单赚币与智能套利能在相同 90 天、相同资金口径下比较；\n11\t3. 未知成本保持未知，不被错误当成 0；\n12\t4. 收益评估严格只读，不创建 OKX 策略，也不修改同步、回补或 Portfolio 状态。\n13\t\n14\t测试通过只代表“计算链路可以用于 Shadow 观察和小额实验决策”，不代表策略未来能赚钱，更不代表已经达到 10%–20% 年化目标。\n15\t\n16\t| 层级 | 验证内容 | 能证明 | 不能证明 |\n17\t|---|---|---|---|\n18\t| 自动化测试 | 公式、修订选择、参数约束、数据库行为 | 实现符合计算契约 | OKX 当前产品值得购买 |\n19\t| 历史情景分析 | 过去 90 天资金费与人工成本假设 | 该窗口的可比结果 | 无前视偏差的真实回测 |\n20\t| Shadow 观察 | 连续记录当时可见的费率、成本和建议 | 建议是否稳定、输入是否可获得 | 真实成交和退出成本 |\n21\t| 2,000–5,000 USDT 小额验证 | 实际成交、资金费、再平衡、退出和净收益 | 模型与真实结果的偏差 | 可直接扩大到 200,000 USDT |\n22\t\n23\t必须按顺序推进。历史结果即使很好，也只能进入小额验证。\n24\t\n25\t## 2. 固定测试口径\n26\t\n27\t| 项目 | 值 | 说明 |\n28\t|---|---:|---|\n29\t| 历史窗口 | `[2026-05-20T00:00:00Z, 2026-08-18T00:00:00Z)` | 恰好 90 天 |\n30\t| 候选资金 | 20,000 USDT | 情景资金，不是实盘授权 |\n31\t| 简单赚币 APR | 3.5% | 用户提供；实盘前重新核对 OKX 确认页 |\n32\t| 智能套利空头名义 | 19,047.61 USDT | OKX 策略预览截图 |\n33\t| 聚合开仓成本 | 36.001 USDT | OKX 策略预览截图 |\n34\t| 期末策略 | 全部退出回 USDT | 与简单赚币同口径 |\n35\t\n36\t简单赚币 90 天基准收益：\n37\t\n38\t```text\n39\t20,000 × 3.5% × 90 / 365 = 172.602739... USDT\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t显示值应为 `172.60 USDT`。\n43\t\n44\t## 3. 准备环境并运行自动化测试\n45\t\n46\t```bash\n47\tcd /Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/ai-crypto-arbitrage\n48\tcp .env.example .env                 # 仅首次运行；填写本地 MySQL 密码\n49\tdocker compose --env-file .env up -d mysql\n50\tdocker compose --env-file .env ps    # 等待 mysql 变为 healthy（业务账户已执行 SELECT 1）\n51\t\n52\tset -a\n53\tsource .env\n54\tset +a\n55\t\n56\tmvn test\n57\tmvn -DskipTests package\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t当前基线预期 `68/68` 通过，并生成 `target/ai-crypto-arbitrage-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar`。测试使用 Testcontainers MySQL 8.4，不会清空本地开发数据库。"},"output":"1\t# 第一期测试手册\n2\t\n3\t> 适用范围：简单赚币与 BTC 智能套利的 90 天收益评估。现货网格尚未实现，不在本手册验收范围内。\n4\t\n5\t## 1. 测试目标与边界\n6\t\n7\t本轮只验证四件事：\n8\t\n9\t1. 程序能正确读取 OKX 已实现资金费率事实；\n10\t2. 简单赚币与智能套利能在相同 90 天、相同资金口径下比较；\n11\t3. 未知成本保持未知，不被错误当成 0；\n12\t4. 收益评估严格只读，不创建 OKX 策略，也不修改同步、回补或 Portfolio 状态。\n13\t\n14\t测试通过只代表“计算链路可以用于 Shadow 观察和小额实验决策”，不代表策略未来能赚钱，更不代表已经达到 10%–20% 年化目标。\n15\t\n16\t| 层级 | 验证内容 | 能证明 | 不能证明 |\n17\t|---|---|---|---|\n18\t| 自动化测试 | 公式、修订选择、参数约束、数据库行为 | 实现符合计算契约 | OKX 当前产品值得购买 |\n19\t| 历史情景分析 | 过去 90 天资金费与人工成本假设 | 该窗口的可比结果 | 无前视偏差的真实回测 |\n20\t| Shadow 观察 | 连续记录当时可见的费率、成本和建议 | 建议是否稳定、输入是否可获得 | 真实成交和退出成本 |\n21\t| 2,000–5,000 USDT 小额验证 | 实际成交、资金费、再平衡、退出和净收益 | 模型与真实结果的偏差 | 可直接扩大到 200,000 USDT |\n22\t\n23\t必须按顺序推进。历史结果即使很好，也只能进入小额验证。\n24\t\n25\t## 2. 固定测试口径\n26\t\n27\t| 项目 | 值 | 说明 |\n28\t|---|---:|---|\n29\t| 历史窗口 | `[2026-05-20T00:00:00Z, 2026-08-18T00:00:00Z)` | 恰好 90 天 |\n30\t| 候选资金 | 20,000 USDT | 情景资金，不是实盘授权 |\n31\t| 简单赚币 APR | 3.5% | 用户提供；实盘前重新核对 OKX 确认页 |\n32\t| 智能套利空头名义 | 19,047.61 USDT | OKX 策略预览截图 |\n33\t| 聚合开仓成本 | 36.001 USDT | OKX 策略预览截图 |\n34\t| 期末策略 | 全部退出回 USDT | 与简单赚币同口径 |\n35\t\n36\t简单赚币 90 天基准收益：\n37\t\n38\t```text\n39\t20,000 × 3.5% × 90 / 365 = 172.602739... USDT\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t显示值应为 `172.60 USDT`。\n43\t\n44\t## 3. 准备环境并运行自动化测试\n45\t\n46\t```bash\n47\tcd /Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/ai-crypto-arbitrage\n48\tcp .env.example .env                 # 仅首次运行；填写本地 MySQL 密码\n49\tdocker compose --env-file .env up -d mysql\n50\tdocker compose --env-file .env ps    # 等待 mysql 变为 healthy（业务账户已执行 SELECT 1）\n51\t\n52\tset -a\n53\tsource .env\n54\tset +a\n55\t\n56\tmvn test\n57\tmvn -DskipTests package\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t当前基线预期 `68/68` 通过，并生成 `target/ai-crypto-arbitrage-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar`。测试使用 Testcontainers MySQL 8.4，不会清空本地开发数据库。"}}}}],"updated_at":"2026-10-26T15:02:40.159Z","cumulative_token_usage":{"input_tokens":44010,"output_tokens":8992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":164928,"total_tokens":217930},"cumulative_cost":{"amount":0.527314,"currency":"USD"},"request_token_usage":{"7760c593-4eb4-4236-8186-4d64a012d3b1":{"input_tokens":44010,"output_tokens":8992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":164928,"total_tokens":217930}},"acpx":{"current_model_id":"default","available_models":["default","opus","sonnet","haiku"],"model_control":"config_option","config_options":[{"id":"mode","name":"Mode","description":"Session permission mode","category":"mode","type":"select","currentValue":"default","options":[{"value":"auto","name":"Auto","description":"Use a model classifier to approve/deny permission prompts"},{"value":"default","name":"Manual","description":"Standard behavior, prompts for dangerous operations"},{"value":"acceptEdits","name":"Accept Edits","description":"Auto-accept file edit operations"},{"value":"plan","name":"Plan Mode","description":"Planning mode, no actual tool execution"},{"value":"dontAsk","name":"Don't Ask","description":"Don't prompt for permissions, deny if not pre-approved"},{"value":"bypassPermissions","name":"Bypass Permissions","description":"Bypass all permission checks"}]},{"id":"model","name":"Model","description":"AI model to use","category":"model","type":"select","currentValue":"default","options":[{"value":"default","name":"Default (recommended)","description":"glm-5.3[1m]"},{"value":"opus","name":"glm-5.3","description":"Custom Opus model"},{"value":"sonnet","name":"glm-5.3","description":"Custom Sonnet model"},{"value":"haiku","name":"glm-4.7-air","description":"Custom Haiku model"}]},{"id":"effort","name":"Effort","description":"Available effort levels for this model","category":"thought_level","type":"select","currentValue":"default","options":[{"value":"default","name":"Default"},{"value":"low","name":"Low"},{"value":"medium","name":"Medium"},{"value":"high","name":"High"},{"value":"xhigh","name":"Xhigh"},{"value":"max","name":"Max"}]}],"available_commands":[{"name":"deep-research","description":"Deep research harness — fan-out web searches, fetch sources, adversarially verify claims, synthesize a cited report. (dynamic workflow)","has_input":false},{"name":"design-sync","description":"Push a React design system to claude.ai/design. This runs a converter that bundles the real component code (from Storybook or a bare package) and uploads it. Use when the user runs /design-sync or says \"sync my design system to Claude Design\".","has_input":true},{"name":"dataviz","description":"Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \"chart\", \"graph\", \"plot\", \"data viz\", \"visualization\", \"dashboard\", \"analytics\", \"visualize data\", \"categorical colors\", \"sequential / diverging palette\", \"stat tile\", \"sparkline\", \"heatmap\", \"legend\", \"axis\", \"tooltip\", \"chart colors\", \"color by series\".","has_input":false},{"name":"update-config","description":"Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.","has_input":false},{"name":"verify","description":"Verify that a code change actually does what it's supposed to by exercising it end-to-end and observing behavior — drive the affected flow, not just tests or typecheck. Run before committing nontrivial changes; bootstraps this repo's project verify skill if none exists yet. Don't invoke it on a diff that only touches tests, docs, or other code with no runtime surface to drive (a change to product source always has one) — there's nothing to observe.","has_input":false},{"name":"debug","description":"Enable debug logging for this session and help diagnose issues","has_input":true},{"name":"code-review","description":"Review the current diff, or a PR number/branch/path target, for correctness bugs and reuse/simplification/efficiency cleanups at the given effort level (low/medium: fewer, high-confidence findings; high→max: broader coverage, may include uncertain findings); with no level given, it reuses the level you typed last. Pass --comment to post findings as inline PR comments, or --fix to apply the findings to the working tree after the review.","has_input":true},{"name":"simplify","description":"Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.","has_input":true},{"name":"batch","description":"Research and plan a large-scale change, then execute it in parallel across 5–30 isolated worktree agents that each open a PR.","has_input":true},{"name":"fewer-permission-prompts","description":"Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.","has_input":false},{"name":"loop","description":"Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace.","has_input":true},{"name":"claude-api","description":"Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \"looks like a one-liner\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/computer-use; generate/summarize/extract/classify/rewrite/converse over NL; debugging refusals/cutoffs/streaming/tool-calls/tokens).\nSKIP only when another provider is being worked on (overrides all triggers): OpenAI/GPT/Gemini/Llama/Mistral/Cohere/Ollama named in the query; OR `grep -rE 'openai|langchain_openai|google.generativeai|genai|mistralai|cohere|ollama'` over the project hits (run this grep FIRST if no provider named — don't Read the file).","has_input":false},{"name":"run","description":"Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).","has_input":false},{"name":"run-skill-generator","description":"Author or improve the run-<unit> skill — a per-project skill that tells agents how to build, launch, and drive this project's app. Use when the user asks to set up the project, get it running, write run instructions, or verify build/run steps work from a clean environment.","has_input":false},{"name":"agents","description":"(removed) Ask Claude to create/manage subagents, or edit .claude/agents/","has_input":false},{"name":"auto-mode-setup","description":"Set up and customise auto mode — environment context, plus optional rule tweaks","has_input":true},{"name":"autocompact","description":"Configure the auto-compact window size","has_input":true},{"name":"compact","description":"Free up context by summarizing the conversation so far","has_input":true},{"name":"config","description":"Set a setting by key","has_input":true},{"name":"context","description":"Show current context usage","has_input":false},{"name":"effort","description":"Set effort level for model usage","has_input":true},{"name":"fast","description":"Toggle fast mode (Opus 5)","has_input":true},{"name":"heapdump","description":"Dump the JS heap to ~/Desktop","has_input":false},{"name":"init","description":"Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation","has_input":false},{"name":"mcp","description":"Manage MCP servers","has_input":true},{"name":"import","description":"Import config from another AI coding agent","has_input":false},{"name":"model","description":"Set the AI model for Claude Code","has_input":true},{"name":"__remote-workflow","description":"Run the workflow script delivered in this session environment (server-launched sessions only)","has_input":false},{"name":"workflow-launch-exec","description":"Execute a server-launched workflow handoff (workflow_launch event sessions only)","has_input":false},{"name":"reload-skills","description":"Pick up skills added or changed on disk during this session","has_input":false},{"name":"rename","description":"Rename the current conversation","has_input":true},{"name":"security-review","description":"Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","has_input":false},{"name":"usage","description":"Show session cost, plan usage, and what's contributing to your limits","has_input":false},{"name":"insights","description":"Generate a report analyzing your Claude Code sessions","has_input":false},{"name":"recap","description":"Generate a one-line session recap now","has_input":false},{"name":"skill-doctor","description":"Show which loaded skills are unused and costing context","has_input":false},{"name":"goal","description":"Set a goal — keep working until the condition is met","has_input":false},{"name":"design","description":"Grant or revoke Claude agent access to your Design projects","has_input":true},{"name":"design-consent","description":"Grant Claude agent access to your Design projects","has_input":false},{"name":"design-revoke","description":"Revoke Claude agent access to your Design projects","has_input":false},{"name":"list-agents","description":"List subagents and other Claude sessions you can message","has_input":false},{"name":"team-onboarding","description":"Help teammates ramp on Claude Code with a guide from your usage","has_input":false}],"session_options":{"allowed_tools":["Read","Grep","Glob"],"claude_execution_policy_ref":".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793026771764/execution-authority/claude-execution-policy.json","claude_execution_policy_sha256":"1e73de364f491dd6e4e103007f35c777673ca6185cbc710c5929e4c4f7f99ebc"}}}
